repo that resolves from no clone.\n\nBOUNDARY (checked by class census before filing): distinct from CF-074 (complete-row artifacts must resolve from a published ref) and CF-144 (tree_fp instruments disagree) because this is a TYPE-SHAPE failure on PENDING rows that breaks consumers before resolvability is even reachable; distinct from CF-045/CF-084 (CF-011/CF-013 cite one pruned absolute scratch log) because those are resolvability, not shape; distinct from CF-199 (the ACCEPTANCE-PLAN pin names an unpublished commit) which is about a pin's resolvability, not a field's type. Counts re-measured with jq immediately before this append at the tip above.","acceptance_criteria":"0. AC0 — reproduce on the current tree from the repo root: this row's `probe` (extracted with `jq -r 'select(.id==\"CF-200\").probe' .coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl`) prints `detail_null=29 detail_object=144 detail_string=2`, `evidence_array=76 evidence_string=4`, four `STRING_EVIDENCE` lines (CF-172, CF-173, CF-174, CF-179), two `STRING_DETAIL` lines (CF-128, CF-130), `control_array_iterate_rc=0`, `defect_evidence_iterate_rc=4`, `defect_detail_iterate_rc=4`, `validator_rc=0 detail_evidence_warnings=0`, and exits 0.\n1. AC1 — the WRITER refuses the shape: a staged `bash scripts/boardctl create` whose detail is a bare string, and one whose `detail.evidence` is a bare string, both exit non-zero and print a named refusal that names the offending field, while a conforming row is still accepted; the refusal must be a named row/message, not a traceback.\n2. AC2 — `bash scripts/boardctl validate` gains the shape check and is RED today: at 2bb114f it exits non-zero and names CF-128, CF-130, CF-172, CF-173, CF-174, CF-179. After repair the same command prints `RESULT: OK`.\n3. AC3 — the six rows are repaired byte-preservingly (every untouched line identical; the board diff is keys-on-those-lines only, not a whole-file reserialisation), each carrying a `detail` object and, where evidence exists, a `detail.evidence` array of objects with `run_id`/`ts`/`tree_fp`/`artifacts`; the probe's `STRING_*` lines are gone and `detail_string=0 evidence_string=0`.\n4. AC4 — every artifact cited by those rows resolves from the published ref: `git cat-file -e origin/main:<artifact>` succeeds for each, and no row cites a path outside the repository (no `~/.hermes/...`, no absolute host path). This clause binds only the four rows named here; the complete-row resolvability class stays with CF-074 and CF-050.\n5. AC5 — `bash tests/selftest.sh` gains an arm that is RED against today's shape (a fixture row with `detail` as a string must make the new check print its named failure) and GREEN after the repair, and `bash tests/selftest.sh` prints `SELFTEST: PASS`.\n6. AC6 — the shape contract is documented where the writer's contract lives (docs/traceability-doctrine.md, which CF-047 owns for the field meanings), stating the required types for `detail` and `detail.evidence` and the command that checks them, without restating CF-047's field-by-field resolution rules.","probe":"F=.coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl; T=$(mktemp); echo \"detail_null=$(jq -s '[.[]|select((.detail|type)==\"null\")]|length' \"$F\") detail_object=$(jq -s '[.[]|select((.detail|type)==\"object\")]|length' \"$F\") detail_string=$(jq -s '[.[]|select((.detail|type)==\"string\")]|length' \"$F\")\"; echo \"evidence_array=$(jq -s '[.[]|select((.detail|type)==\"object\" and ((.detail.evidence|type)==\"array\"))]|length' \"$F\") evidence_string=$(jq -s '[.[]|select((.detail|type)==\"object\" and ((.detail.evidence|type)==\"string\"))]|length' \"$F\")\"; jq -r 'select((.detail|type)==\"string\") | \"STRING_DETAIL \\(.id) \\(.status) \\(.detail)\"' \"$F\"; jq -r 'select((.detail|type)==\"object\" and ((.detail.evidence|type)==\"string\")) | \"STRING_EVIDENCE \\(.id) \\(.status) \\(.detail.evidence)\"' \"$F\"; jq -e 'select(.id==\"CF-197\") | .detail.evidence[]' \"$F\" >/dev/null 2>&1; echo \"control_array_iterate_rc=$?\"; jq -e 'se