 {"id":"CF-201","title":"P3 — a row is closed on the lane's own criterion, not on the row's acceptance criteria: CF-198 closed complete at 2bb114f on a hand edit while its AC1 demanded a committed checker the tree does not contain","status":"pending","priority":"P3","complexity":3,"reasoning":"Measured 2026-11-04 by the code-factory-duckbrain-pm tick (09-20-35) at published tip 2bb114f.\n\nCF-198 was closed complete at 2bb114f on implementation commit e7a248c and verdict run efce6b5c (CF-198-DOC1, passed true). Three facts, each a command:\n\n1. The closing diff touches documentation only: `git show --name-status --format= e7a248c` prints `M docs/ACCEPTANCE-PLAN.md` and `A docs/audits/code-factory-docs-2026-11-04-cf198-section-map.md`. No test file, no script.\n2. The row at that tip required artifacts that commit does not contain: `git show 2bb114f:.coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl | jq -r 'select(.id==\"CF-198\").acceptance_criteria' | grep -c 'DERIVED by a committed checker'` prints 1, while the tree carries no such checker — `git ls-tree -r --name-only 2bb114f docs/audits/ | grep -c cf198-section-mapping` prints 0 and `git show 2bb114f:tests/selftest.sh | grep -c cf198` prints 0.\n3. The criterion that was actually graded never mentions that requirement: `git show 2bb114f:.gitreins/history/2026-11-04/efce6b5c/verdict.json | jq -r .task_criteria | grep -c 'DERIVED by a committed checker'` prints 0, and its own text closes the door explicitly — \"Out of scope, do NOT grade: closing board row CF-198, the verdict binding\".\n\nSo tier 1 and tier 2 both passed, the board validator answered RESULT: OK, and nothing in the repository could fail: the judge grades the criterion string the closing lane wrote, not the row it is closing. A lane can therefore satisfy a weaker criterion than its own row demands, and the acceptance criteria become decoration.\n\nThis is the class the same tick had to repair (the superseding landing 210389f adds exactly the checker and the §39 arm the DOC1 close skipped), but it outlives that row: `grep -rn 'task_criteria' scripts/ tests/ docs/audits/` finds no consumer, so no shipped check compares a graded criterion with the row it closed.\n\nDistinct from CF-074 (closure evidence that does not RESOLVE in the tree — efce6b5c resolves fine), CF-047 (the doctrine does not define detail.evidence fields), CF-181 (a verdict bound to a commit that is on no branch) and CF-191 (a Tier-1 PASS recorded beside a non-zero test-command exit). Here every artifact resolves, the judge is honest about what it graded, and the row is still closed against a criterion that omits half of its acceptance criteria.","acceptance_criteria":"1. A committed checker (path free, re-runnable from the repository root) takes the board path and a git ref and, for every COMPLETE row whose newest evidence entry cites a .gitreins/history/<date>/<run>/verdict.json that resolves in that tree, extracts the verdict task_criteria and fails — exit nonzero, naming the row id, the run directory and the NUMBER of the acceptance-criteria item it could not find — while any numbered item of that row's acceptance_criteria is absent from every criterion string of that verdict under whitespace-normalized, case-sensitive substring comparison. Rows that predate the check are grandfathered only through a committed, dated exception list that names each row id and a reason, and an exception for a row closed after the check lands is itself a failure.\n\n2. The same checker exits 0 only when every non-grandfathered complete row either has its numbered acceptance-criteria items covered by the graded criterion or carries an explicit criterion_coverage: \"none:<reason>\" entry, and a fixture proves both directions: a synthetic board+verdict pair whose criterion omits item 2 must print a NAMED failure naming the row and item 2 and exit nonzero, while the same pair with the item quoted must exit 0. Quote both runs; do not assert the substring FAIL alone.\n\n3. The check is wired into tests/selftest.sh as its own numbered section, with the red arm executed before the green one and its output quoted, so a future weakening of the check reds the suite.\n\n4. The full run at the closing commit names today's measured divergence rather than passing silently: it must report the CF-198 closure at 2bb114f / run efce6b5c as a criterion that omits its AC1 and AC2 wording, and that row must either be re-graded against its own acceptance criteria or carry an appended evidence entry recording the criterion gap. No earlier closed row may be silently exempted: every exemption is an entry in the committed exception list with a date and a reason.\n\n5. Gate and publication at the closing commit: bash tests/selftest.sh prints SELFTEST: PASS, bash scripts/boardctl validate prints RESULT: OK, and after the push git rev-list --left-right --count origin/main...HEAD prints 0 0.","probe":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T10:44:07Z","updated_at":"2026-11-04T10:44:07Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"6d4bb0df0132ed05155634cd33ecdfad5e98ecc9de6e27a0f25d8211887d0049"},"capability_tags":["board","gitreins","evidence"]}
